          "payload": {
            "text": "I don’t have a specific chair choice recorded — your memories show you’re redecorating the office but not which desk chair you settled on.\n\nIf you want to jog your memory or decide now, quick questions will help:\n- Budget (roughly)?  \n- How many hours/day do you sit? Any back/neck issues?  \n- Preferred style (modern/minimal, executive leather, mid-century, sporty/gaming)?  \n- Flooring type (hardwood/carpet) and preferred color/material?\n\nQuick recommendations by use-case to help you decide:\n- Best ergonomics (all-day work): mesh or fully adjustable ergonomic chair (e.g., Steelcase Leap, Herman Miller Aeron or more affordable Autonomous/ErgoChair). Good lumbar support, adjustable seat depth/armrests, breathable mesh.  \n- Executive look (formal, leather): high-back leather or faux-leather chair — comfortable and stylish but check lumbar support if you sit long hours.  \n- Budget-friendly / occasional use: basic ergonomic task chair (adjustable height, tilt lock) — ok for shorter sessions.  \n- Stylish / light-duty (matches redecorating aesthetics): upholstered mid-century or designer task chair — looks great but may lack advanced ergonomics.  \n- If you want a mix of comfort + style: mid-range ergonomic with fabric upholstery (adjustable lumbar + headrest).\n\nTell me your answers to the short questions above and I’ll:\n- Recommend 2–3 exact models that match your budget/style, or  \n- Draft an email to order or ask a supplier questions, or  \n- Save your final choice as a note/reminder (if you want me to create a draft/email to yourself for future reference). Which would you like to do next?"
