            "text": "I don't have a specific icebreaker recorded for your team building event — your memories show you're planning the event but not which game you chose.\n\nIf you want, here are concise, easy-to-run icebreaker options (with when they work best). Pick one and I can give a script, materials list, or add it to your agenda.\n\nQuick options\n- Two Truths and a Lie — low-prep, great for small-to-medium groups; helps people learn fun facts.\n- Human Bingo — good for mingling in-person; gets everyone moving and talking.\n- Speed Networking / Lightning Intros — scalable for larger groups; quick 1–1 rotations to surface connections.\n- Marshmallow Challenge (team build) — 15–30 min, hands-on problem solving and teamwork (in-person).\n- Scavenger Hunt — flexible (in-person or hybrid); energizing and collaborative.\n- Show & Tell (object that represents you) — personal, low-pressure, works well for new or remote teams.\n- Office Trivia or Team Facts Quiz — fun, fosters shared history and culture.\n- Common Ground (find things everyone in the small group has in common) — fast, builds rapport and empathy.\n- Photo or Playlist Icebreaker — remote-friendly; ask people to share a photo/track and why.\n\nTell me:\n- Is the event in-person, virtual, or hybrid?\n- Team size?\n- Time available for the icebreaker (5, 15, 30+ minutes)?\n- Tone: fun/energetic, deep/reflective, or problem-solving?\n\nI’ll recommend the best match and can:\n- Give step-by-step instructions and timing,\n- Draft an agenda or an invite message to attendees,\n- Save your chosen icebreaker as a note so you don’t forget.\n\nWhich direction would you like to go?"
